00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.600 align:start position:0%
what bearing does faith have on the  lives of people in today's world world  shaped by the processes of globalization  now we can talk about faith as  represented by faith traditions but  always faith is carried on by  individuals and individuals that are in  particular way challenged by this  question our political leaders how shall  shall they bring their own faith  perspectives to bear upon their own  public life are the risks involved in  being identified as persons of faith can  they in some way craft and shape  ethically based politics that is shaped  by the way in which they themselves  believe what are the compromises in  which they maybe have to be engaged as  they do so in order to take into account  the complex realities of the world in  which they find themselves what are the  means of resolving conflicts between the  claims of the faith and the demands of  the concrete situation in which they  find themselves the issue is really  complicated even more if we think that  in many places in the world  globalization processes are increasingly  bringing people of various religious  persuasions and some who do not believe  at all into a common space now it's not  just a matter of asking the question how  individual faith is brought to bear in  public life but how is it brought to  bear in the pluralistic settings where  different people have different visions  comprehensive visions of common life and  moral life in general and they vie and  want to insert themselves in their own  perspectives into common life these are  issues on which the health and  prosperity and stability and peace of  our common world depend and politicians  often are at the heart of those issues  especially those who them  elves are persons of faith
 

